{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794229115,"nonce":"Ntjt6YethRtaQ+MVodtyALx0/V4=","title":"A bound class or attribute re-matches every rule against the node and its whole subtree","message":"`sync_dynamic_classes` runs on every full build. For each `class_when` /\n`attr_when` class, `add_class_layer` matched every stateless rule against the\nnode twice (before and after registering the class), and\n`add_class_everywhere` did the same for every descendant. A cn tab panel\ncarries `data-state`, so the code editor's whole subtree was matched against\nthe full cn stylesheet twice per build.\n\nMeasured on the russl toy (release, headless, 1400x860): a steady full rebuild\ntook ~35 ms; a `sample` profile put nearly all of the CPU in\n`complex_selector_matches` / `compound_matches` / `has_class` under\n`reconcile_dynamic_classes`.\n\nFix: only rules that name the class can start matching. The node is re-matched\nagainst rules naming it in the subject compound; descendants against rules\nnaming it in an earlier compound, and are skipped when there are none. An\nattribute counts by name; `:not`/`:is`/`:has` and attribute-read states\n(`:checked`, `:disabled`) count conservatively. The full rule list is computed\nonly for a node that gained rules, to build its layer. Steady rebuild ~15 ms\nafter.","files":null}]}